## Plan

1. **Read the spec.** `bd show {{ .Bead }}`. A spec whose notes already carry a `{{ .PlanMarker }}` block has been planned: comment that and write outcome `pass`. Done when the five sections are in hand.
2. **Propose the children.** Each child is one unit of work a single polecat can land in one branch, written in the standard bead shape an operator's spec uses:
   - **Goal** — what the child makes true, in one or two lines.
   - **Constraints** — the files and packages it may touch, and what it must leave alone.
   - **Out of scope** — what a reader might expect and will not find.
   - **Gate** — the command that proves it, usually `make gate`.
   - **Size** — one worker, one landing.
   Add the child's acceptance criteria as a `- [ ]` checklist, and its dependencies on the other children by their position in this proposal. `gt bead dep add A B` means A needs B: a child that cannot be built until another has landed depends on that one, and being listed later is not by itself a dependency. Done when every child has all five lines, a checklist and a deps line.
3. **Write the block into the notes.** Append one block to `{{ .Bead }}`:

```bash
gt bead note {{ .Bead }} "$(cat <<'PROPOSAL'
{{ .PlanMarker }}
Spec: {{ .Bead }}
Children: 2

1. <the child's title>
Goal: <what the child makes true>
Constraints: <files and packages, and what it must leave alone>
Out of scope: <what it excludes>
Gate: make gate
Size: one worker, one landing
Acceptance: - [ ] <the check that proves it>; - [ ] <another check>
Deps: none

2. <the child's title>
<the same lines>
Deps: 1
PROPOSAL
)"
```

   The first line is `{{ .PlanMarker }}` and nothing else: it is how a reader, and the steward's own scan, tells a planned spec from an unplanned one. The quoted delimiter keeps the shell out of the text; for a proposal too long even for that, write it to a file and pass it: `gt bead note {{ .Bead }} "$(cat proposal.txt)"`. Done when `bd show {{ .Bead }}` prints the block under the notes.
4. **Report.** `gt bead comment {{ .Bead }} "{{ template "steward-tag" . }} PLAN 2 children proposed: <their titles>"`, then write the verdict file. Done when `bd show {{ .Bead }}` lists your comment.

